!GLWindow
=========

Example 2: a spinning triangle in a desktop window. Move it, resize it, cover it up; close it to quit.

Click Menu over the window for two speed options:
  Hardware overlay   the display shows the frames itself (Raspberry Pi,
                     with the VideoOverlay module)
  Draw at 240x180    draw a quarter of the pixels and stretch the picture
                     to fill the window
The title bar says how the frames are reaching the screen: "plotted"
(the usual way: the computer copies each frame into the window),
"overlay", or "overlay hidden" while something is over the window
(including this menu). The overlay starts a moment after you choose it.

Built from window.c in the riscos-mesa devkit's examples folder; read the
comments in that file to see how it works.

Needs: RISC OS 5, an ARMv7 or later processor (Raspberry Pi 2, 3 or 4,
or a Cortex-A8/A9/A15 board), and SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport
from PackMan.

